   "id": 1003,
   "chapter": 10,
   "name": "What is a rate?",
   "fullName": "Rate: comparing quantities of different kinds",
   "lesson": {
    "heading": "Rate: comparing quantities of different kinds",
    "sub": "Chapter 10 · Topic 3",
    "body": "<div class=\"g4-hero\"><img class=\"g4-stk \" src=\"/assets/stickers/scales.webp\" srcset=\"/assets/stickers/scales@2x.webp 2x\" alt=\"\"><p>A <strong>rate</strong> compares two amounts of <strong>different kinds</strong>, such as rand and kilograms. \"R20 per kg\" is a rate.</p></div><div class=\"def-box\"><div class=\"def-box-title\">📖 Rate</div><p>We use the word <strong>per</strong> (or a slash): R12 per kg = R12/kg, 60 km per hour = 60 km/h. A rate tells you how much for <strong>one</strong>: one kilogram, one hour, one apple.</p></div><div class=\"example-box\"><div class=\"example-box-title\">✏️ Oranges</div><div class=\"example-step\"><span class=\"step-num\">1</span><span>2 oranges cost R3.</span></div><div class=\"example-step\"><span class=\"step-num\">2</span><span>R3 = 300 cents. 300c ÷ 2 = 150c.</span></div><div class=\"example-step\"><span class=\"step-num\">3</span><span>The cost of 1 orange = <strong>150 cents</strong> (R1,50).</span></div></div><div class=\"example-box\"><div class=\"example-box-title\">✏️ Apples at R2,50 each</div><div class=\"example-step\"><span class=\"step-num\">1</span><span>R2,50 = 250c.</span></div><div class=\"example-step\"><span class=\"step-num\">2</span><span>2 apples: 2 × 250c = 500c = <strong>R5,00</strong>. 3 apples: 3 × 250c = 750c = <strong>R7,50</strong>.</span></div><div class=\"example-step\"><span class=\"step-num\">3</span><span>10 apples: 10 × 250c = 2 500c = <strong>R25,00</strong>.<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px auto;font-size:18px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:center;border:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.35);font-weight:800\">Apples</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:center;border:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.35);\">1</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:center;border:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.35);\">2</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:center;border:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.35);\">3</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:center;border:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.35);\">10</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:center;border:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.35);font-weight:800\">Cost</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:center;border:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.35);\">R2,50</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:center;border:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.35);\">R5,00</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:center;border:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.35);\">R7,50</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:center;border:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.35);\">R25,00</td></tr></table></span></div></div><div class=\"g4-sim\" id=\"g4-s1003\"><h4>🎮 Price Table</h4><p class=\"how\">A rate tells you the price of ONE. Find it, then use it for any number.</p><div class=\"g4-big\" data-k=\"goal\" style=\"font-size:22px\"></div><table class=\"g4-chart\" data-k=\"tbl\" style=\"margin:8px auto\"></table><div class=\"g4-row\"><button class=\"g4-btn\" data-k=\"check\">Check</button><button class=\"g4-btn ghost\" data-k=\"new\">New one</button></div><div class=\"g4-out\" data-k=\"out\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div><script>window.G4 = Object.assign(window.G4 || {}, {\n  fmt: n => String(n).replace(/\\B(?=(\\d{3})+(?!\\d))/g, '\\u00a0'),\n  stk: (name, cls) => '<img class=\"g4-stk ' + (cls || '') + '\" src=\"/assets/stickers/' + name + '.webp\" srcset=\"/assets/stickers/' + name + '@2x.webp 2x\" alt=\"\">',\n  rnd: (a, b) => a + Math.floor(Math.random() * (b - a + 1)),\n  num: s => { const v = parseInt(String(s).replace(/[\\s\\u00a0]/g, ''), 10); return isNaN(v) ? null : v; },\n  q: (root, k) => root.querySelector('[data-k=\"' + k + '\"]'),\n  pt: (svg, e) => { const p = svg.createSVGPoint(); p.x = e.clientX; p.y = e.clientY; return p.matrixTransform(svg.getScreenCTM().inverse()); },\n  shuffle: a => { for (let i = a.length - 1; i > 0; i--) { const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1)); [a[i], a[j]] = [a[j], a[i]]; } return a; }\n});\n{ const __rev = o => { for (const k in o) if (o[k] && o[k].__fn) o[k] = (0, eval)('(' + o[k].__fn + ')'); return o; };\n(function (L, root) {\n  const { q, rnd, shuffle } = window.G4;\n  const out = q(root, 'out'), tb = q(root, 'tbl');\n  const R = c => 'R' + Math.floor(c / 100) + ',' + String(c % 100).padStart(2, '0');\n  const parse = s => { s = String(s).replace(/[\\s ]/g, '').replace(/^r/i, ''); if (!s) return null; if (/c$/i.test(s)) { const v = parseInt(s, 10); return isNaN(v) ? null : v; } const v = parseFloat(s.replace(',', '.')); return isNaN(v) ? null : Math.round(v * 100); };\n  let P = null;\n  function fresh() {\n    const it = L.items[rnd(0, L.items.length - 1)], k = rnd(2, 4), unit = rnd(it.lo, it.hi) * 50;\n    const cols = [1].concat([k].concat(shuffle([5, 6, 10, 3, 8].filter(v => v !== k)).slice(0, 2)).sort((x, y) => x - y)), gi = cols.indexOf(k);\n    P = { it, k, unit, cols, gi };\n    q(root, 'goal').innerHTML = L.goal(k, it.n, R(k * unit)) + ' ' + window.G4.stk(it.s, 'sm');\n    const inp = i => '<input class=\"g4-input\" data-k=\"c' + i + '\" inputmode=\"decimal\" style=\"width:120px;text-align:center\" aria-label=\"' + cols[i] + '\">';\n    tb.innerHTML = '<tr><th>' + L.num + '</th><th>' + L.cost + '</th></tr>' + cols.map((c, i) => '<tr><td style=\"font-size:24px\">' + c + '</td><td style=\"padding:4px 8px\">' + (i === gi ? '<span style=\"font-size:22px\">' + R(k * unit) + '</span>' : inp(i)) + '</td></tr>').join('');\n    out.className = 'g4-out'; out.innerHTML = L.ask;\n  }\n  function check() {\n    const msgs = []; let all = true;\n    P.cols.forEach((c, i) => {\n      if (i === P.gi) return;\n      const el = q(root, 'c' + i), v = parse(el.value), ok = v === c * P.unit;\n      el.style.borderColor = v == null ? '' : ok ? '#4ade80' : '#f87171';\n      if (!ok) { all = false; if (v != null) msgs.push(i === 0 ? L.tip1(R(P.k * P.unit), P.k) : L.tipN(c)); }\n    });\n    out.className = 'g4-out ' + (all ? 'good' : 'bad');\n    out.innerHTML = all ? L.yes(R(P.unit), P.it.one) : (msgs.length ? msgs.join('<br>') : L.fill);\n  }\n  root.addEventListener('click', e => { const t = e.target.closest('button'); if (!t) return; if (t.dataset.k === 'check') check(); else if (t.dataset.k === 'new') fresh(); });\n  root.addEventListener('keydown', e => { if (e.key === 'Enter' && e.target.tagName === 'INPUT') check(); });\n  fresh();\n})(__rev({\"items\":[{\"n\":\"apples\",\"one\":\"apple\",\"s\":\"apple\",\"lo\":3,\"hi\":6},{\"n\":\"bananas\",\"one\":\"banana\",\"s\":\"banana\",\"lo\":2,\"hi\":5},{\"n\":\"mealies\",\"one\":\"mealie\",\"s\":\"mealie\",\"lo\":6,\"hi\":12},{\"n\":\"juice boxes\",\"one\":\"juice box\",\"s\":\"juice-box\",\"lo\":10,\"hi\":20},{\"n\":\"ice creams\",\"one\":\"ice cream\",\"s\":\"ice-cream\",\"lo\":12,\"hi\":24}],\"num\":\"Number\",\"cost\":\"Cost\",\"goal\":{\"__fn\":\"(k, n, p) => '<b>' + k + ' ' + n + '</b> cost <b>' + p + '</b>.'\"},\"ask\":\"First find the cost of 1. Then use it to fill in the rest of the table. You can type R2,50 or 250c.\",\"tip1\":{\"__fn\":\"(p, k) => 'Cost of 1 = ' + p + ' ÷ ' + k + '. Tip: change to cents first.'\"},\"tipN\":{\"__fn\":\"c => 'Cost of ' + c + ' = ' + c + ' × the cost of 1.'\"},\"fill\":\"Fill in every empty box.\",\"yes\":{\"__fn\":\"(u, one) => 'All correct! The rate is <b>' + u + ' per ' + one + '</b>. Each cost is the number × ' + u + '.'\"}}), document.getElementById('g4-s1003')); }</script><div class=\"tip-box\"><span class=\"tip-icon\">💡</span><span>Ratio or rate? If both amounts have the same unit (cm and cm), it is a ratio. If the units are different (rand and kg), it is a rate.</span></div>"
   },
